    "description": "A thelodont, a small jawless fish about 7 cm long from the Late Silurian of Saaremaa, Estonia, known from complete, articulated bodies. Instead of bony plates it was covered in thousands of tiny, tooth-like scales. It had a rounded head with a small mouth at the front, flap-like fins behind the gills, a tall dorsal fin and a big tail, and fed on small particles near the sea floor."
