    "description": "One of the most primitive osteostracans, jawless armoured fish about 20 cm long from the Silurian of Scotland and Norway. Its broad, horseshoe-shaped head shield was a mosaic of small bony tiles, with the eyes close together on top. Behind the shield it had a pair of flap-like pectoral fins, among the oldest true paired fins of any animal, the beginnings of our own arms. It grubbed for food on the sea floor."
