    "description": "A small galeaspid, a jawless armoured fish a few centimetres long from the early Silurian of Zhejiang, China. It had a rounded, horseshoe-shaped bony head shield with the eyes on top and a slit-like opening on its snout. Its braincase, preserved in fine detail and studied with X-ray scans, showed how the nose and brain of early vertebrates were arranged before jaws evolved. It strained food from the mud of shallow seas."
